 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "This guided work is an enquiry into the arts of the region where your school is.\nSteps:\n1. Choose a question: Which arts are practised here? Who makes them? What are they used for?\n2. Prepare questions for an interview.\n3. Visit artisans (carvers, potters, weavers, blacksmiths, bead makers, musicians) or a museum or palace, with permission and an adult.\n4. Observe and record: the materials (wood, clay, raffia, beads, bronze), the tools, the steps, the uses, the meaning of symbols. Take notes, sketches or photographs (with permission).\n5. Sort the information and write a short report with a title, an introduction, findings, a conclusion and the names of the people interviewed.\nRespect: ask before photographing sacred objects; thank the people you interview.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "a": "a wood carver"
  },
  "problem": "Write three questions to ask {a} in your enquiry.",
  "steps": [
   "Ask about materials and tools: Which wood and tools do you use?",
   "Ask about meaning and use: What are your carvings used for, and what do the symbols mean? Who taught you?"
  ],
  "answer": "Which wood and tools do you use? What are your carvings used for? Who taught you the craft?",
  "checks": []
 },
